            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "southern CONUS",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "During the El Ni\u00f1o phase, the subtropical Pacific jet stream extends towards the southern CONUS, leading to above-average precipitation. Conversely, during La Ni\u00f1a, the Pacific jet stream tends to meander northward. This northward shift results in enhanced precipitation in the Pacific Northwest, while the southern CONUS experiences below-average rainfall. In these regions, the phase of ENSO serves as a robust predictor of the precipitation anomalies (Patricola et al. 2020; O'Brien et al. 2019; L'Heureux et al. 2015).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
